# Bentley R-Type standard steel saloon, 1952-1955.
#
# The last separate-chassis Bentley before the S-series: 4,566 cc six, 5,182 mm
# long, 1,778 mm wide, 1,651 mm high, 3,048 mm wheelbase. 2,323 standard steel
# saloons built, plus 208 Continentals. The R-Type was the Bentley-bodied
# equivalent of the Rolls-Royce Silver Dawn.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bentley_R_Type
#
# Colours: Black, Silver, Maroon and Grey were period Bentley finishes.
#
# Weight: 12 in total (black 5, silver 3, maroon 2, grey 2). Section F: the
# 1940s-50s class-4 row, alongside the S1 and the Silver Cloud I.
#
# Speed 160 km/h (about 100 mph); comfort 85/458 (line). Classes 3,4.
# Dates: 1952-1955 with a road tail to about 1978.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bentley-r-type.blend. References:
# citycars/references/bentley-r-type/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

